  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_convolution_operation(image: list, kernel: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **2D Convolution from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_convolution_operation(image: list, kernel: list) -> list:\n    img, k = np.array(image, dtype=float), np.array(kernel, dtype=float)\n    oh, ow = img.shape[0] - k.shape[0] + 1, img.shape[1] - k.shape[1] + 1\n    out = np.zeros((oh, ow))\n    for i in range(oh):\n        for j in range(ow): out[i, j] = np.sum(img[i:i+k.shape[0], j:j+k.shape[1]] * k)\n    return np.round(out, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
